          "prompt_tps": 23.1,
          "prompt_tokens": 1248,
          "completion_tokens": 132,
          "reasoning_chars": 0,
          "content": "</ifm|think_faster>In one paragraph: A heat pump is an air-source heating and cooling system that moves thermal energy rather than generating it \u2014 in cooling mode, it uses a compressor, condenser, expansion valve, and evaporator to draw heat from indoor air and release it outdoors, cooling your home; in heating mode, it runs the same cycle in reverse, pulling heat from the relatively warmer outdoor air (or ground) and transferring it inside, so even on cool days it can efficiently heat a space while simultaneously cooling the outside air, with the system's efficiency measured by its coefficient of performance (COP), which indicates how much heat is delivered per unit of electricity consumed.",
